  ('sap-btp', 'In SAP Integration Suite, what is ''Gather step''?', '["A paid add-on only available in Integration Suite Enterprise", "An on-premise only SAP Process Orchestration feature", "A deprecated SAP PI/XI mapping type no longer supported", "an iFlow step that collects split sub-messages back into a single aggregated message"]', 3, 'an iFlow step that collects split sub-messages back into a single aggregated message', 'integration-intro', 1631),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which Integration Suite term describes: ''an iFlow step that collects split sub-messages back into a single aggregated mes''?', '["XSLT mapping", "Splitter step", "HTTP adapter", "Gather step"]', 3, 'Gather step: an iFlow step that collects split sub-messages back into a single aggregated message', 'integration-intro', 1632),
  ('sap-btp', 'What is the hierarchical structure of SAP BTP accounts from top to bottom?', '["Global Account → Directory → Subaccount", "Subaccount → Global Account → Directory", "Directory → Subaccount → Global Account", "Global Account → Subaccount → Directory"]', 0, 'BTP accounts nest: Global Account (top) → optional Directories → Subaccounts (bottom). Entitlements flow down; workloads live in subaccounts.', '0-sp-test', 1633),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which Cloud Foundry component is responsible for running application instances?', '["Cell", "Controller", "Router", "UAA"]', 0, 'CF Cells host the containers (warden/garden) where actual app instances run. The Controller manages lifecycle; the Router handles ingress.', '0-sp-test', 1634),
  ('sap-btp', 'What is the maximum number of Cloud Foundry app instances you can scale to in BTP trial?', '["3", "1", "10", "Unlimited"]', 0, 'BTP trial limits CF apps to 3 instances total across all apps to prevent resource abuse.', '0-sp-test', 1635),
  ('sap-btp', 'In Cloud Foundry, what file format is used to declare environment-specific variables alongside manifest.yml?', '["vars.yml", "env.json", ".env", "config.yaml"]', 0, 'CF supports a `vars.yml` file used with `cf push --vars-file vars.yml` for environment-specific value injection.', '0-sp-test', 1636),
  ('sap-btp', 'What does BTP''s ''Free Tier'' offer compared to a ''Trial'' account?', '["Free Tier services are time-unlimited; Trial has a 90-day expiry", "Free Tier is only for enterprise customers", "Trial gives more compute quota than Free Tier", "Free Tier requires a credit card; Trial does not"]', 0, 'BTP Free Tier plans do not expire, unlike the 90-day trial. They have quota limits but are permanently available.', '0-sp-test', 1637),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which SAP BTP environment supports serverless functions via the Kyma runtime?', '["Kyma", "Cloud Foundry", "ABAP", "HTML5"]', 0, 'Only the Kyma environment provides serverless (Function) workloads alongside microservices on Kubernetes.', '0-sp-test', 1638),
  ('sap-btp', 'What Kubernetes resource type does Kyma use to expose HTTP services externally?', '["APIRule", "Service", "Ingress", "Route"]', 0, 'Kyma uses a custom CRD called APIRule (backed by Istio and an API Gateway) to expose services via HTTP/HTTPS.', '0-sp-test', 1639),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which SAP BTP tool provides a visual low-code interface for building SAP Fiori apps without coding?', '["SAP Build Apps", "SAP Business Application Studio", "SAP Fiori Tools", "SAP AppGyver Classic"]', 0, 'SAP Build Apps (formerly AppGyver) provides a visual drag-and-drop low-code app builder on BTP.', '0-sp-test', 1640),
  ('sap-btp', 'In BTP, what is the purpose of a ''Directory''?', '["To group multiple subaccounts for shared management and budget monitoring", "To store static files for HTML5 apps", "To run CF workloads at a higher resource tier", "To configure global routing for BTP services"]', 0, 'Directories group subaccounts under a global account for shared cost centre management and hierarchical administration.', '0-sp-test', 1641),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which BTP service must be enabled before you can deploy Multi-Target Applications via `cf deploy`?', '["Cloud Foundry MTA Deploy Service plugin", "SAP Build Work Zone", "SAP Continuous Integration & Delivery", "SAP LeanIX"]', 0, 'The CF MTA Deploy Service (cf-deploy plugin + MTA backend service in CF) is required to process .mtar archives.', '0-sp-test', 1642),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which CAP annotation enables draft functionality on an entity so users can save incomplete records?', '["@odata.draft.enabled: true", "@cds.draft: enabled", "@draft.mode: true", "@UI.Drafts: true"]', 0, 'The CDS annotation `@odata.draft.enabled: true` activates the CAP draft protocol for an entity, enabling save/edit/activate workflows.', 'cap-intro', 1643),
  ('sap-btp', 'In CAP, how do you express a to-many association from Orders to Items?', '["items: Composition of many Items on items.order = $self", "items: Association to Items", "items: many Items", "items: Array of Items"]', 0, 'CAP uses `Composition of many TargetEntity on backlink = $self` for owned to-many relationships.', 'cap-intro', 1644),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which CAP handler registers code that runs instead of the default database CRUD operation?', '["on()", "before()", "after()", "around()"]', 0, '`on()` replaces the default handler. `before()` and `after()` run around it but don''t replace it.', 'cap-handlers', 1645),
  ('sap-btp', 'What does `cds.env.requires.db.kind = ''hana''` in package.json configure?', '["Sets HANA Cloud as the production database for the CAP project", "Installs the hana npm package automatically", "Enables HANA-specific SQL syntax in the CDS editor", "Connects the CAP project to a local HANA Express installation"]', 0, 'Setting `cds.requires.db.kind = ''hana''` tells the CAP runtime to use HANA Cloud via the @sap/hana-client driver in production.', 'cap-intro', 1646),
  ('sap-btp', 'In CAP CDS, what does the `aspect cuid` provide?', '["Adds a UUID primary key field named ''ID''", "Adds createdAt and modifiedAt timestamps", "Adds soft-delete support via deletedAt field", "Adds a sequential integer auto-increment ID"]', 0, 'The `cuid` aspect adds `key ID: UUID` to an entity. Use `managed` for audit timestamps.', 'cap-intro', 1647),
  ('sap-btp', 'What is the CAP command to run the app locally while it uses live cloud services instead of SQLite?', '["cds watch --profile hybrid", "cds serve --cloud", "cds run --live", "cds start --remote"]', 0, '`cds watch --profile hybrid` uses the hybrid profile which reads .env bindings created by `cds bind` to connect to live services.', 'cap-intro', 1648),
  ('sap-btp', 'In CAP, which folder should custom service handler JavaScript files be placed in?', '["srv/", "db/", "app/", "lib/"]', 0, 'Service handlers (.js files with same name as .cds service files) live in the `srv/` folder alongside the service definitions.', 'cap-intro', 1649);
INSERT INTO public.assessment_questions
  (course_id, question, options, correct_option, explanation, topic_slug, order_num)
VALUES
  ('sap-btp', 'Which CDS type is used for currency amounts that require an associated currency code field?', '["cds.Decimal", "type Currency", "sap.common.Currency", "String"]', 0, 'CAP provides the `sap.common.Currencies` value list and a `cds.Decimal` with currency association for proper amount handling.', 'cap-intro', 1650),
  ('sap-btp', 'What does `SELECT.from(Books).where({stock: {''>'': 0}})` return in a CAP handler?', '["A CQL query object that returns books with stock greater than zero", "An immediate SQL result", "A promise that deletes all books with zero stock", "A filtered view definition"]', 0, 'CAP''s CQL (CDS Query Language) `SELECT.from().where()` builds a query object that is lazily executed when awaited.', 'cap-handlers', 1651),
  ('sap-btp', 'In CAP, what is the difference between `reject` and `error` on the request object?', '["reject() aborts the request; error() only logs a non-fatal message", "reject() is for client errors; error() is for server errors", "They are identical — both abort the request", "error() rolls back; reject() does not"]', 0, '`req.reject(400, ''msg'')` throws an HTTP error stopping the request. `req.error(''msg'')` collects non-fatal errors shown as messages.', 'cap-handlers', 1652),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which annotation makes a CAP entity read-only via the OData service?', '["@readonly", "@insertonly", "@cds.autoexpose: false", "@restrict: [{grant: ''READ''}]"]', 0, '`@readonly` prevents CREATE/UPDATE/DELETE via the generated OData endpoints for that entity.', 'cap-odata', 1653),
  ('sap-btp', 'What is the purpose of `using from ''@sap/cds/common''` in a CDS model?', '["Imports reusable aspects like cuid, managed, Country, Currency from the SAP common model", "Loads the SAP CAP runtime into the project", "Imports Bootstrap CSS for the UI layer", "Connects to the SAP Common Data Model in SAP Analytics Cloud"]', 0, '@sap/cds/common provides standard CDS definitions like `cuid`, `managed`, `sap.common.Countries` and `sap.common.Currencies`.', 'cap-intro', 1654),
  ('sap-btp', 'In CAP OData V4, what does `$expand=items($select=product,quantity)` do?', '["Inlines the items association and returns only product and quantity fields", "Expands all entities and selects the first two columns", "Filters items where product equals quantity", "Returns items sorted by quantity descending"]', 0, 'OData `$expand` inlines associated data. The nested `$select` restricts which fields of the expanded entity are returned.', 'cap-odata', 1655),
  ('sap-btp', 'What CAP command adds the Approuter npm module and xs-app.json to a project?', '["cds add approuter", "npm install @sap/approuter", "cds init --approuter", "cf add-route approuter"]', 0, '`cds add approuter` scaffolds the approuter sub-project with xs-app.json and updates mta.yaml automatically.', 'cap-intro', 1656),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which CAP feature allows sending events between services without direct coupling?', '["Messaging via cds.emit / cds.on", "REST callback URLs", "WebSockets via socket.io", "SAP Push Notification Service"]', 0, 'CAP''s built-in messaging lets services emit and subscribe to events using `cds.emit(''EventName'', data)` and `srv.on(''EventName'', ...)`.', 'cap-handlers', 1657),
  ('sap-btp', 'In SAPUI5, which method do you call to navigate to a route named ''detail'' with parameter id=''42''?', '["this.getRouter().navTo(''detail'', {id:''42''})", "this.navigate(''detail'', {id:''42''})", "sap.ui.getCore().navTo(''detail'')", "this.getOwnerComponent().getRoute(''detail'').display()"]', 0, 'Router.navTo(routeName, parameters) is the standard navigation method in SAPUI5 controllers.', 'ui5-routing', 1658),
  ('sap-btp', 'What does `{path: ''MyModel>/items'', templateShareable: false}` configure in an XML view?', '["An aggregation binding to the ''items'' array of a named model ''MyModel''", "A one-time property binding", "A filter on the items array", "A sorter for the items collection"]', 0, 'Aggregation bindings use `path: ''ModelName>/arrayPath''`. The `templateShareable: false` prevents template reuse across bindings.', 'ui5-binding', 1659),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which SAPUI5 lifecycle hook is the correct place to set up models and fetch initial data?', '["onInit", "onBeforeRendering", "onAfterRendering", "onExit"]', 0, '`onInit` fires once when the controller is created — the right place to set models. Avoid DOM operations here; use `onAfterRendering` for those.', 'ui5-lifecycle', 1660),
  ('sap-btp', 'In SAPUI5, how do you create a JSON model with initial data `{count: 0}`?', '["new sap.ui.model.json.JSONModel({count: 0})", "new sap.ui.model.JSONModel({count: 0})", "sap.ui.model.json.create({count: 0})", "JSONModel.load({count: 0})"]', 0, 'The full require path is `sap/ui/model/json/JSONModel` but in sap.ui.define it resolves to `sap.ui.model.json.JSONModel`.', 'ui5-binding', 1661),
  ('sap-btp', 'What does the `xmlns:core=''sap.ui.core''` declaration in an XML view enable?', '["Using sap.ui.core controls like <core:Fragment> with the ''core'' prefix", "Importing a CSS library from sap.ui.core", "Registering a custom namespace for the project", "Enabling sap.ui.core routing in the view"]', 0, 'XML namespace declarations map prefixes to SAPUI5 libraries so you can use `<core:Icon>`, `<core:Fragment>`, etc.', 'ui5-intro', 1662),
  ('sap-btp', 'In a SAPUI5 formatter, what must the function return to update the bound control property?', '["The transformed value to display", "A jQuery DOM element", "A boolean true/false only", "An sap.ui.model.type.* instance"]', 0, 'Formatters receive raw model values and return the display value. Any type is valid — string, boolean, sap.ui.core.ValueState, etc.', 'ui5-binding', 1663),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which SAPUI5 control is used to show a full-screen dialog-like page within the same app flow?', '["sap.m.NavContainer", "sap.m.Popover", "sap.m.Dialog", "sap.m.SplitApp"]', 0, 'sap.m.NavContainer (and its subclass sap.m.App) hosts multiple pages and lets you navigate between them in-app without a dialog.', 'ui5-controls', 1664),
  ('sap-btp', 'What does `data-sap-ui-compatVersion=''edge''` in the SAPUI5 bootstrap script do?', '["Enables the latest SAPUI5 behaviour without backwards-compatibility restrictions", "Locks the app to the current patch version", "Disables deprecated APIs", "Forces the app to use the sap_belize theme"]', 0, 'compatVersion=''edge'' opts into the most current behaviour of the framework rather than legacy-compatible defaults.', 'ui5-intro', 1665),
  ('sap-btp', 'In SAPUI5, what is the standard way to define a reusable UI fragment?', '["Create an .fragment.xml file and load it with Fragment.load({name: ''...''})", "Add a <Template> tag inside the view XML", "Extend sap.ui.core.Fragment in a JS file", "Use sap.ui.require with type ''fragment''"]', 0, 'Fragments are standalone XML (or JS) files loaded via `Fragment.load({name:''com.myapp.view.MyFragment'', controller: this})`.', 'ui5-controls', 1666),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which SAPUI5 binding mode makes the model the single source of truth and never propagates UI changes back?', '["OneWay", "TwoWay", "OneTime", "ReadOnly"]', 0, 'OneWay: model→UI only. TwoWay: UI changes propagate back to the model. OneTime: binds once, then disconnects.', 'ui5-binding', 1667),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which OData annotation renders a button in the Fiori Elements List Report toolbar?', '["@UI.LineItem with #DataFieldForAction", "@UI.SelectionFields", "@UI.PresentationVariant", "@Common.FieldControl"]', 0, '`@UI.LineItem` entries with `$Type: ''UI.DataFieldForAction''` create toolbar buttons triggering an OData action.', 'fiori-elements', 1668),
  ('sap-btp', 'In Fiori Elements Object Page, which annotation groups fields into a collapsible section?', '["@UI.Facets with ReferenceFacet", "@UI.LineItem", "@UI.HeaderFacets", "@UI.QuickViewFacets"]', 0, '`@UI.Facets` with `ReferenceFacet` pointing to a `FieldGroup` annotation creates named sections on the Object Page.', 'fiori-elements', 1669),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which CDS annotation enables the smart variant management in a Fiori Elements List Report?', '["@UI.PresentationVariant", "@UI.Manifest.variant: true", "@UI.SmartVariantManagement: true", "@sap.fe.enableVariants: true"]', 0, 'Not directly a CDS annotation — variant management in FE is controlled by the manifest''s `variantManagement` setting, but `@UI.PresentationVariant` controls default sorting/grouping.', 'fiori-elements', 1670),
  ('sap-btp', 'What annotation makes a Fiori Elements table column show a rating indicator (stars)?', '["@UI.DataPoint with Visualization: #Rating", "@UI.StarRating", "@Common.Stars", "@UI.RatingIndicator"]', 0, '`@UI.DataPoint` with `Visualization: #Rating` renders a star rating control in the table column.', 'fiori-elements', 1671),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which annotation in CAP/Fiori provides a dropdown value help from a fixed list of values?', '["@Common.ValueList with CollectionPath", "@UI.SelectOptions", "@cds.enum", "@UI.ParameterDefaultValue"]', 0, '`@Common.ValueList` with a `CollectionPath` pointing to an entity (or an inline `Parameters` list) provides dropdown value helps.', 'fiori-elements', 1672),
  ('sap-ai', 'In SAP AI Core, what is an ''Execution'' and how does it differ from a ''Deployment''?', '["Execution is a batch training/inference run; Deployment is a persistent online serving endpoint", "Execution is a deployed model; Deployment is the training run", "They are identical — both serve models in real time", "Execution is scheduled; Deployment is manual"]', 0, 'Executions run to completion (training, batch inference). Deployments stay running to serve online prediction requests.', 'sap-ai-intro', 1673),
  ('sap-ai', 'What is the Generative AI Hub in SAP AI Launchpad?', '["A managed proxy for accessing LLMs like GPT-4o and Claude via a uniform API", "A fine-tuning service for training custom SAP language models", "A document search engine built on SAP HANA vectors", "A chatbot builder for SAP Fiori apps"]', 0, 'Generative AI Hub provides a unified API to access multiple LLM providers (Azure OpenAI, AWS Bedrock, etc.) with SAP-managed governance.', 'sap-ai-genai', 1674),
  ('sap-ai', 'What is ''grounding'' in the context of SAP AI Launchpad orchestration?', '["Augmenting LLM prompts with relevant document content retrieved from a vector store", "Training an LLM on SAP-specific terminology", "Removing hallucinations by validating against a relational database", "Grounding LLM outputs in SAP ERP transaction data"]', 0, 'Grounding retrieves relevant chunks from a vector database and injects them into the LLM prompt as context — the core of RAG pipelines.', 'sap-ai-genai', 1675),
  ('sap-ai', 'Which component in AI Core holds credentials for reading training data from SAP BTP Object Store?', '["Object Store Secret", "Docker Registry Secret", "Resource Group", "Artifact"]', 0, 'The Object Store Secret stores S3-compatible credentials so AI Core executions can read datasets and write model artifacts.', 'sap-ai-intro', 1676),
  ('sap-ai', 'In LLM prompting, what does ''temperature = 0'' mean for a model''s output?', '["The model always picks the highest-probability next token — fully deterministic", "The model is not running and returns no output", "The model hallucinates more at low temperature", "Temperature 0 disables the system message"]', 0, 'Temperature 0 makes the model deterministic — it always picks the most probable token. Higher values increase randomness and creativity.', 'sap-ai-genai', 1677),
  ('sap-ai', 'What is RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)?', '["A technique that retrieves relevant documents and includes them in the LLM prompt to ground answers", "A method that trains the LLM on new data in real time", "An SAP architecture pattern for replacing humans with AI agents", "A HANA in-memory indexing algorithm"]', 0, 'RAG retrieves relevant context from a vector database and injects it into the prompt, allowing the LLM to answer questions from private knowledge without fine-tuning.', 'sap-ai-genai', 1678),
  ('sap-ai', 'What does ''few-shot prompting'' mean?', '["Including 2–5 example input-output pairs in the prompt to guide the LLM''s format and style", "Training the model on a few hundred examples", "Running the model with very short prompts", "Using a small context window to reduce cost"]', 0, 'Few-shot prompting provides examples directly in the prompt so the LLM understands the expected output format without retraining.', 'sap-ai-genai', 1679),
  ('sap-ai', 'In SAP AI Core, what does a ''serving template'' YAML define?', '["How to deploy and configure a model server container as an AI Core Deployment", "How to run a training workflow pipeline", "How to define the schema of an AI Core Artifact", "How to register a Docker registry in AI Core"]', 0, 'Serving templates describe the container image, resource requests, environment variables and ports for running an online model endpoint in AI Core.', 'sap-ai-intro', 1680),
  ('sap-ai', 'Which AI Core API endpoint creates a new deployment from a configuration?', '["POST /v2/lm/deployments", "PUT /v2/lm/deployments/create", "POST /v2/lm/configurations/deploy", "GET /v2/lm/deployments/{id}/start"]', 0, 'POST /v2/lm/deployments with a configurationId body creates a new AI Core Deployment from an existing Configuration.', 'sap-ai-intro', 1681),
  ('sap-btp', 'In SAP HANA Cloud, what does the ''Data Lake Files'' storage add-on provide?', '["Cost-effective cold storage for large unstructured files alongside HANA in-memory data", "A relational table store with slower but cheaper indexing", "A backup service for HANA row store tables", "A file server for HTML5 applications"]', 0, 'HANA Cloud Data Lake provides an S3-compatible cold storage layer tightly integrated with HANA for tiering large/old data cheaply.', 'hana-intro', 1682),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which SQL function in SAP HANA returns the current server timestamp with timezone?', '["CURRENT_UTCTIMESTAMP", "NOW()", "SYSDATE", "GETDATE()"]', 0, 'HANA uses `CURRENT_UTCTIMESTAMP` for UTC time. `CURRENT_TIMESTAMP` gives local server time. GETDATE/NOW are not valid in HANA SQL.', 'hana-intro', 1683),
  ('sap-btp', 'What is the purpose of the `USING COLUMN TABLES` hint in a HANA SQL script?', '["Forces the query planner to use column-store tables for the operation", "Converts row tables to column tables permanently", "Creates an in-memory snapshot of the table", "Enables parallel execution of DML statements"]', 0, 'HANA query hints can guide the optimizer, but column vs row store is actually set at table creation time, not via hints.', 'hana-intro', 1684),
  ('sap-btp', 'In CAP with HANA, what does `hdbcds` artifact type compile from CDS entities?', '["HANA Core Data Services format for HDI container deployment", "A JavaScript class for HANA connection pooling", "An EDMX OData metadata file", "A HANA stored procedure definition"]', 0, 'CDS entities compile to `.hdbcds` (or `.hdbtable`) artifacts that HDI deploys into HANA Cloud containers.', 'hana-intro', 1685),
  ('sap-btp', 'What SAP tool provides a SQL console directly in the browser for HANA Cloud?', '["SAP HANA Database Explorer", "SAP BAS SQL Editor", "SAP HANA Cockpit Query Tool", "SAP DBaaS Console"]', 0, 'SAP HANA Database Explorer (DBX) is a browser-based SQL console, catalog browser and data viewer for HANA Cloud instances.', 'hana-intro', 1686),
  ('sap-btp', 'In SAP Integration Suite, which adapter sends outbound HTTP POST requests to external REST APIs?', '["HTTP Receiver Adapter", "SOAP Sender Adapter", "HTTPS Outbound Connector", "REST Dispatcher"]', 0, 'The HTTP Receiver Adapter configures outbound connections to external HTTP/HTTPS REST endpoints from an iFlow.', 'integration-intro', 1687),
  ('sap-btp', 'What does the ''Content Modifier'' step in an iFlow do?', '["Creates, reads or updates message headers, exchange properties or the message body", "Transforms XML using an XSLT stylesheet", "Routes messages based on conditions", "Splits a multipart message into individual messages"]', 0, 'Content Modifier is the most general-purpose iFlow step for setting or reading metadata and payload in the message pipeline.', 'integration-intro', 1688),
  ('sap-btp', 'In Integration Suite, what is an ''iFlow''?', '["A graphical artifact defining the full message exchange between sender and receiver", "A pre-built connector to SAP S/4HANA", "A JavaScript file running in the Cloud Integration runtime", "An API product published on the API Management portal"]', 0, 'An Integration Flow (iFlow) is the core artifact of Cloud Integration: a visual diagram of steps that process, route and transform messages.', 'integration-intro', 1689),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which Integration Suite capability allows you to create an API proxy that adds rate limiting and auth to an existing backend?', '["API Management", "Cloud Integration", "Event Mesh", "Open Connectors"]', 0, 'API Management creates API proxies that add policies (rate limiting, OAuth, analytics) on top of existing backend services.', 'integration-intro', 1690),
  ('sap-btp', 'What file format do iFlow artifacts use when exported from Integration Suite?', '[".zip (containing BPMN XML and metadata)", "iflow.json", "artifacts.yaml", ".war (Web Application Archive)"]', 0, 'iFlow artifacts export as .zip files containing the BPMN 2.0 XML model, manifest, and any attached scripts/mappings.', 'integration-intro', 1691),
  ('sap-btp', 'In BTP XSUAA, what is the difference between a ''Scope'' and a ''Role Collection''?', '["A Scope is a fine-grained permission string; a Role Collection groups Roles (which bundle Scopes) and is assigned to users", "They are identical — both are assigned directly to users", "A Role Collection is a technical token claim; a Scope is a UI permission", "Scopes apply to services; Role Collections apply to users only"]', 0, 'Scopes are low-level permission strings in JWT tokens. Roles bundle scopes. Role Collections group roles and are assigned to BTP users.', '0-sp-test', 1692),
  ('sap-btp', 'What is ''Principal Propagation'' in the context of SAP Cloud Connector?', '["Forwarding the authenticated BTP user''s identity to on-premise systems without re-authentication", "Creating a new principal in the on-premise system for each BTP user", "Synchronising on-premise users to BTP''s Identity Provider", "Passing API keys from BTP to on-premise SAP systems"]', 0, 'Principal Propagation lets the Cloud Connector pass the BTP user''s identity (as a short-lived X.509 certificate) to on-premise ABAP/ICM.', '0-sp-test', 1693),
  ('sap-btp', 'In OAuth2, which grant type should a background service use when no user is involved?', '["Client Credentials", "Authorization Code", "Resource Owner Password", "Implicit"]', 0, 'Client Credentials grant issues tokens based on the client''s own credentials — correct for machine-to-machine scenarios with no user session.', '0-sp-test', 1694),
  ('sap-btp', 'What does the `@requires: ''authenticated-user''` annotation on a CAP service entity enforce?', '["Only authenticated users with a valid JWT can access the entity", "The entity requires a CAP custom authentication middleware", "Only admin users can read the entity", "The entity is excluded from the OData metadata document"]', 0, 'CAP interprets `@requires: ''authenticated-user''` as a built-in restriction that rejects anonymous access with HTTP 401.', 'cap-intro', 1695),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which BTP service issues the OAuth2 JWT tokens that CAP and approuter validate?', '["SAP Authorization and Trust Management (XSUAA)", "SAP Identity Authentication (IAS) directly", "SAP Credential Store", "SAP Cloud Logging"]', 0, 'XSUAA (SAP Authorization and Trust Management Service) issues JWT access tokens. IAS can federate into XSUAA but XSUAA signs the final token.', '0-sp-test', 1696),
  ('sap-btp', 'What is the purpose of `mbt build` in an MTA-based BTP project?', '["Compiles all MTA modules and packages them into a single .mtar archive for deployment", "Runs unit tests across all MTA modules", "Generates the mta.yaml descriptor automatically", "Deploys the application to Cloud Foundry"]', 0, '`mbt build` uses the MTA Build Tool to compile each module (npm install, cds build, etc.) and pack everything into a deployable .mtar archive.', '0-sp-test', 1697),
  ('sap-btp', 'In an MTA, what does the `requires` section of a module entry define?', '["The resources (services) or other modules this module depends on at runtime", "The npm packages to install before build", "The CF routes this module will use", "The build command to run for this module"]', 0, 'MTA `requires` lists dependencies — service instances or other modules — that must be bound/available when this module deploys.', '0-sp-test', 1698),
  ('sap-btp', 'What does SAP Continuous Integration and Delivery (CI/CD) service on BTP provide?', '["A managed Jenkins-based pipeline service for building, testing and deploying BTP apps", "A local Git server for storing source code", "A code review platform for CAP projects", "An automated testing tool that simulates Fiori user interactions"]', 0, 'SAP CI/CD service provides pre-configured Jenkins pipelines (SAP Cloud SDK Pipeline) as a managed BTP service — no Jenkins admin needed.', '0-sp-test', 1699);
INSERT INTO public.assessment_questions
  (course_id, question, options, correct_option, explanation, topic_slug, order_num)
VALUES
  ('sap-btp', 'In the CF manifest.yml, what does the `memory` field control?', '["The RAM allocated per instance of the CF application", "The total storage quota for all CF apps", "The disk space for buildpack cache", "The shared memory pool across all instances"]', 0, '`memory: 256M` allocates 256 MB RAM per instance. All instances of the app share the same memory setting.', '0-sp-test', 1700),
  ('sap-btp', 'Which Cloud Foundry command shows the last 100 lines of logs from a deployed app?', '["cf logs myapp --recent", "cf tail myapp -n 100", "cf show-log myapp --lines 100", "cf log myapp --history"]', 0, '`cf logs myapp --recent` streams the last buffered log lines. Without `--recent` it streams live logs until Ctrl+C.', '0-sp-test', 1701),
